From c4ac0b6415d59a400a23e19c8982ab53726f8761 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 14:29:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ui): stand the model, stock and fixtures on the viewport
 floor

The ground grid and the bottom of a mill work envelope were drawn at
world Z=0, so a model drawn about its centre showed half under the
floor and a vise placed under the stock showed below it. The new
crate::floor::floor_z puts the floor at the lowest point of the drawn
bodies (models, the shown setups' fixtures, the active stock). With a
fixture the floor is the fixture base and the model and stock stand
on it; removing the fixture brings the floor back to the stock. Undo
and redo follow, because the floor is read from the world each frame.

Display only: no stored position, WCS, toolpath, check or posted
record changes. A lathe keeps its floor at world Z=0.

Fixes #2172

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
